---
import { Code } from "astro/components";
---

<div
  class="col-span-1 lg:col-span-2 rounded-xl bg-card-light dark:bg-card-dark p-6"
>
  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="space-y-3">
    <details class="group">
      <summary
        class="w-full flex justify-between items-center text-left py-2 font-medium cursor-pointer list-none"
      >
        <span>Installation fails with a dependency error. What do I do?</span>
        <span
          class="iconify lucide--chevron-down transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
        ></span>
      </summary>
      <div
        class="pt-2 pb-4 text-subtext-light dark:text-subtext-dark text-sm border-t border-white/10"
      >
        You're missing a dependency duh
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary
        class="w-full flex justify-between items-center text-left py-2 font-medium cursor-pointer list-none"
      >
        <span>How can I have the Bar at top?</span>
        <span
          class="iconify lucide--chevron-down transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
        ></span>
      </summary>
      <div
        class="pt-2 pb-4 text-subtext-light dark:text-subtext-dark text-sm border-t border-white/10"
      >
        <p>
          You either
          <Code
            code={`$ gsettings set com.arkye.morghulis navbar-anchor "top"`}
            lang="sh"
            inline
          />
          or you change it in the QuickMenu and reload Morghulis.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="group">
      <summary
        class="w-full flex justify-between items-center text-left py-2 font-medium cursor-pointer list-none"
      >
        <span>Does Morghulis work with NVIDIA proprietary drivers?</span>
        <span
          class="iconify lucide--chevron-down transition-transform group-open:rotate-180"
        ></span>
      </summary>
      <div
        class="pt-2 pb-4 text-subtext-light dark:text-subtext-dark text-sm border-t border-white/10"
      >
        Yes, Morghulis is compatible with NVIDIA proprietary drivers. Make sure
        you're running the latest driver version for the best experience. Some
        Wayland-specific features may require driver version 495 or newer.
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</div>
